Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.38.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.38.0 (archive 37 feedback): (1) GESTURE-DRIVEN ARC PICKER as requested - the right-edge hot zone is now LOCAL (40x140 at the vertical middle of the right edge, not the whole edge); sliding out of it reveals the semicircular picker, the arc follows the finger up/down, and RELEASING over an app opens it in the float (releasing over empty space just closes the picker); icons shrunk 58->44pt, arc radius 152pt; (2) fixed 'picked an app but saw nothing': a new setFloatVisible: is now shared by the button and the arc, and the arc forces the float visible before hosting (archive 37 proved the user had hidden the float with the button first); (3) fixed 'long-press does not remove': when dockApps was absent the default list was being ADDED instead of removed, so the icon stayed; add/remove now materialise the currently displayed set, so long-press always really removes, and an empty array stays an empty arc; (4) the summon window shrank to a local 88x200 zone at the right-middle (dragging the button moves that whole zone window); (5) diagnostics: onDrag/onResize log their source window class and tag (archive 37 showed UIWindow(tag=2/14) while the status-bar mirror layer 990042 still never fired, because our own level-1100 window covers the same spot).
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
